{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" holds a rule: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"schedule","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" lists the systems of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Declare a System","anchor":"Declare-a-System","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gravity"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also conform a type to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by hand and write its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives the whole world. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for when to do that."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" finds those pairs so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test can keep a schedule free of them."}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Systems","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","required":true,"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" if it may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change anything."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"access","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Access","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","defaultImplementations":1},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"title":"ResourceWriter","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Driving a World from an App","abstract":[{"text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it read results and take part in a step.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"title":"Query","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"title":"ResourceReader","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads a resource."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"CyclicOrdering","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Declaring Systems","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","abstract":[{"text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"title":"Ambiguity","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"EventReader","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"SystemSet","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"title":"ambiguities()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ambiguities"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"UpdateEvents","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has had its chance to read them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"title":"SystemTiming","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Update","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"System","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","abstract":[{"text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"System()","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ForwardEvents","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule can await the events.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"RemovedComponents","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SystemParameter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type a system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system reads and writes."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"required":true,"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"run(in:)","abstract":[{"text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ForwardChanges","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScheduleBuilder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s closure."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScheduledSystem","abstract":[{"text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","abstract":[{"text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interface.","type":"text"}],"title":"MainActorSystem","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"EventWriter","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter"}}}